ate some filmmakers but wright  embraced a chance to work with such a  stacked ensemble cast as he explained to  cinema blend one of wright's favorite  things about the film is the way you can  watch supporting players in every single  shot and see a different version of the  story unfolding as right put it that's  very true to the books in the books  there's this kind of peanut gallery feel  where there's things going on and  nothing going on in the background and  the ensemble is always doing something  in the books i tried to pull that off in  the film as well  scott pilgrim vs the world is a  departure from other edgar wright movies  in several key ways including that the  project had a significantly bigger  budget than prior rights works like  short of the dead however another key  departure from wright's other films was  that this british born filmmaker was  insistent that there were no british  performers in the cast you want to fight  me  for her was that not clear  is that not clear  of course european talent is so  widespread in the acting community that  someone from across the pond was bound  to sneak onto the catalyst for scott  pilgrim versus the world satya baba who  played matthew patel in the film was not  just born in london but grew up in the  same part of london as wright himself  baba's years working in america were  enough to help him keep wright unaware  of his history during the casting  process  one of the performances most critical to  making scott pilgrim vs the world work  as well as it does is ellen wong's turn  as knives chow what could have been a  passive performance the forgettable  other girl to the more prominent ramona  flowers becomes unforgettable in wong's  hands what's especially impressive is  that wong makes sure chow never lapses  into being a mucking caricature even  when she's having a breakdown over scott  pilgrim seeing another older woman wang  injects a relatable quality into child's  character that makes us fully understand  her perspective given just how perfectly  she inhabited this role it can be  shocking to hear that initially one was  convinced she had no chance of securing  the part as she told entertainment  weekly as an asian actress i was never  going out for a role like this this was  not the type of role that i would be  able to even look at thankfully for the  sake of the overall movie wang not only  auditioned for scott pilgrim versus the  world but also scored the part of knives  in the process ensuring this film would  have one of its most important  performances  scott pilgrim vs the world has garnered  varying degrees of responses to its  approach regarding female characters  however one objectively true fact about  the film is that there are several women  in the story beyond scott pilgrim's love  interest from owner flowers and knives  chow played by the likes of brie larson  and aubry plaza among others these  characters and their comedic moments are  some of edgar wright's favorite parts of  this production as he told collider the  thing i'm really pleased about with this  film as opposed to some of the other  comedies out there and even stuff i've  done before is that it has a lot of  funny women in it given how the  characters played by performers like  plaza and larson became some of the most  beloved scene stealers in scott pilgrim  vs the world it's a good thing wright  made time to shine the spotlight on  multiple women in the film  while the widely acclaimed project scott  pilgrim vs the world has like any movie  not been without some criticism most  notably the film was being critiqued for  its casting which largely employed white  actors among those who have registered  grievances with this is brian lee  o'malley who pens the film source  graphic novels an author of french  canadian and korean heritage o'malley  has been open about his issues with the  eventual casting of the scott pilgrim  versus the world movie in a post on his  blog radio meru 