ght recalled in an  interview with entertainment weekly and  then there was this final set piece on a  pyramid suddenly we slowed down to doing  10 shots in a day which is very slow for  me i sat there on top of this pyramid  looking down at these enormous platforms  being maneuvered around and i thought  whose idea was this and it was mine  while the scene itself proved to be  exhilarating to watch unfold in a movie  theater it's apparent that complicated  sets and choreography made it an  enormous undertaking to actually shoot  thankfully for writing company all of  that effort ended up paying off  handsomely since his climactic battle  closed out scott pilgrim versus the  world on an exciting high note  from the very start scott pilgrim vs the  world makes it apparent you're going to  watch something special when a  performance from the band's sex bob-arm  triggers a visually aggressive opening  credit sequence the names of key casts  and crew members are displayed against  frantic animation and a wave of colors  that clue the viewer in on the kind of  visually unpredictable and audacious  movie they're about to absorb in  breaking this sequence down for the art  of the title sequence edgar wright  revealed several fascinating facets of  this segment including that his very  existence came at the suggestion of  quentin tarantino after the pulp fiction  director saw an early screening of the  film the artists in charge of crafting  these opening credits also had to come  up with their own unique visuals they  couldn't draw from imagery in either the  film itself or the scott pilgrim graphic  novels it took an enormous amount of  efforts and craft to pull off such an  unusual approach to an opening credit  sequence but the result was something  that made scott pilgrim versus the world  a captivating experience right from the  start music plays a big part in scott  pilgrim versus the world how could it  not after all scott plays in a band  called sex bob and so many of the film's  big action sequences begin with bands  performing on stage but music's  influence in this film was not just  limited to in-universe performances the  world of musicals also had a significant  influence on how edgar wright composed  the various major action set pieces as  the director told collider we thought it  should play out like a musical in a way  in terms of the fights are not  dissimilar to the songs i always thought  there were a lot of martial arts films  that were like musicals so we wanted to  take that further you see the results on  screen as many of the film's fight  scenes play out like elaborate dance  numbers it was a style right would take  a step further years later with this  musically inspired car chase film baby  driver  in the aftermath of scott pilgrim versus  the world failing to take the box office  by storm the conversation inevitably  turned to what went wrong one recurring  answer as to how such an acclaimed film  failed to click with audiences was to  look at the film's marketing which many  deemed lackluster and a key culprit in  the box office performance of course  those who made the film have their own  thoughts as to what it was like to  advertise such an unorthodox title  speaking to entertainment weekly for the  film's 10th anniversary in 2020 wright  opened up about the disappointment  noting how tempting it was to blame  other people for the failure the  director has been asked numerous times  over the years what the key factor was  for the film's box office disappointment  but he's always been resistant to the  idea that just one thing was responsible  in the end wright just seemed glad that  the film found new life on home video as  he told ew after the film didn't open  well i realized the thing to do is to  take responsibility for it but also just  believe in the fact that it was a good  film and people would find it eventually  and people did indeed find it eventually  today scott pilgrim vs the world is  c